              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One tab in a View area's tab bar, --size-tab-strip high and at most --size-tab-preferred wide: the file-type mark (a diff's comparison mark), the title on one line cut at the tail, a dirty ● in --color-warning, and the toolbar close (System / Icon Button) on the active or hovered tab. A preview's title is italic. The active area's active view sits on --color-background with the --size-tab-indicator accent underline; another area's active view sits on --color-background without it. An unavailable view's title is struck through in --color-muted; the canvas draws the strike as a hairline over the sample title. While dragged, a floating copy on --color-elevated with a hairline border follows the pointer and the tab keeps its place. The tooltip and accessible name carry the kind, the full path, and Preview or Unavailable.",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-caption",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
