              "name": "Spec",
              "fill": "$--subtle-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One message component for a View area's body. The empty Views (the one area left when the last view closes) says no file or diff is open, with Show Explorer while the Explorer is hidden and Open file ⌘P; the layout does not change on its own. A view's own states: Opening… while its file is read; waiting, naming the device state, until its root can be read, after which it reads by itself; unavailable, with the read failure, Close view and Retry. A state belongs to its view; other views and areas are untouched. Buttons follow the shared text button: compact 24 high, body semibold, standard on --color-elevated with a hairline, quiet without a container. The per-view states sit in an area at --size-view-area-min-height, written as its literal 144 (a --size-tab-strip tab bar over a 112 body).",
