    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "pr-card-sheet",
      "x": 8000,
      "y": 7264,
      "name": "Component / PR hover card",
      "width": 480,
      "fill": "$--card",
      "cornerRadius": "$--radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$--spacing-lg",
      "padding": "$--spacing-md",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "pr-card-sheet-title",
          "name": "Title block",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$--spacing-xxs",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pr-card-sheet-title-name",
              "name": "PR hover card (web sidebar c",
              "fill": "$--foreground",
              "content": "PR hover card (web sidebar checkout row)",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-title",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pr-card-sheet-title-spec",
              "name": "The card a checkout row open",
              "fill": "$--subtle-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The card a checkout row opens on hover and keyboard focus in place of its text tooltip (web/src/components/pr-card.tsx, PRD checkout-pr-glyph-card D-03, D-08, D-09, D-12). It is the shell’s tooltip with hoverable content: same delay, stays while the pointer crosses onto it, closes on Escape. The badge line is the pull request’s lifecycle word or its review decision (Open, Draft, Merged, Closed, Approved, Changes requested, Review required), the number, and Open PR, the one control on the card; ⌘ on it opens the default browser. Then the title on up to two lines, a rule, and one row per fact the snapshot has: Review and Checks in their result color, Branch in mono, Agents as the sidebar badge’s marks, Commit as the last commit’s age, Path in mono muted. A row with nothing to say takes no place; a checkout with no pull request has no badge line; a folder that is gone has only Folder missing over its path; a card that would hold one value is the plain text tooltip instead. The row’s glyph is a button only while it is a pull request’s lifecycle, with a ring in that color under the pointer.",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-caption",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "pr-card-sheet-masters",
          "name": "Master",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$--spacing-xs",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pr-card-sheet-masters-name",
              "name": "Master: the card with every ",
              "fill": "$--muted-foreground",
              "content": "Master: the card with every row; each state is a ref",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-micro",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "pr-card",
              "name": "Component / PR hover card",
              "reusable": true,
              "width": 360,
              "fill": "$--popover",
